; T-0111 - presentation: the 2x scale art/STYLE.md specifies.
;
; art/STYLE.md line 15: "A 30x18 board at 32px is 960x576, shown at 2x in a
; 1080p window." A 32 px tile must therefore cover 64 screen pixels. The
; default 1152x648 window drew it at 1x, which is why sprites read as tiny.
;
; 960x540 logical viewport + **windowed** (mode=0) + a 1920x1080 window
; override + canvas_items stretch with aspect "keep" and integer scale_mode: the
; development window is exactly 2x on a screen that can hold it, and every
; element is pixel-crisp. Fullscreen was rejected for the development period
; (the human does not want the game taking over the screen); a release build
; can choose fullscreen later. Aspect "keep" letterboxes rather than distorting,
; which is what keeps 32 px art square.
;
; Presentation only: no sprite, scene size or gameplay constant changes. The
; UI is anchored, so every HUD element is laid out against the 960x540 logical
; rect and is unaffected by the physical surface size. See T-0111.

[display]

window/size/viewport_width=960
window/size/viewport_height=540
window/size/mode=0
window/size/window_width_override=1920
window/size/window_height_override=1080
window/stretch/mode="canvas_items"
window/stretch/aspect="keep"
window/stretch/scale_mode="integer"
